(2) The code must include (in particular) guidance in relation to—
(a) information that should be provided to the interviewee and the accused in
relation to such an interview;
(b) the notification of the accused’s solicitor of such an interview;
(c) the attendance of the interviewee’s solicitor at such an interview;
(d) the attendance of the accused’s solicitor at such an interview;
(e) the attendance of any other appropriate person at such an interview taking into
account the interviewee’s age or any disability of the interviewee.

(3) Any police officer or other person charged with the duty of investigating offences who
arranges or conducts such an interview shall have regard to the code.

(4) In preparing the code, the Secretary of State shall consult—
